# 0102-exported-app-prepares-its-own-shaders.patch -- the owner's field bugs in EXPORTED game apps (player mode). Applies after 0101. With it, outside the patches: crates/ibuilder-pipeline
# src/settings.rs (apply_default_language, launcher_default_language), src/boot.rs (prepare_boot calls it after the settings and env.txt), tests/default_language.rs.
# UNTESTED ON DEVICE: compiled, its pure part ran in the host harness, the Rust in cargo test (below). Field logs read: target/agent-work/splogs (South Park The Stick of Truth, light IPA).
#
# 1. "Preparing the game" for ever. It is GameBootOverlay (over the game view: "Preparing the game m:ss"), which goes away at the first picture it SEES in gameapp.guest.log. It read the log
#    from where it stood when the overlay appeared; an exported app boots fast (the field log: present #1 at 0.19 s), so the first picture was already written and the panel stayed up for its
#    30-minute limit over a game that was running. It now reads from where the log stood when the RUN began (guestLogAtRunStart, BeginRun), checks once at once, and any presented frame ends it
#    (BootOverlayRule: "present #N").
# 2. No shader preparation when the exported app is opened. The export carried the main app's games/<id>/warmed.tsv and prepared.tsv (what the MAIN app's Metal cache holds): the exported
#    app read them as its own (same app build): the field log's "710 libraries ... 0 compiled in 0 s, 710 already warm" and "done". Now: the export leaves this cache state out
#    (warmed.tsv, prepared.tsv, the host's pso_tail.tsv: PlayerWarm.CacheState); an exported app removes the copies an older export set up, and its markers name its own bundle
#    (GameWarm.CacheBuild: "<app build> in <bundle id>"), so another app's markers never count. As soon as it opens, it prepares EVERY library of its game in the background (the run of
#    0076/0086, what was played first), with the lock-screen progress, the player page's line "Preparing the shaders before the first play: N of M (you can play now; it will stutter until
#    done)" and its bar, and "Pause the preparation" / "Resume the preparation" (kept across launches). Play never waits (no "Still preparing the game" question any more): the run stops for
#    the game and goes on at the next opening.
# 3. Never a full preparation before the first frame: the chain counts the seed list alone (profile.rs set_pso_prepare_percent), so a short seed list with a long pso_user.tsv (what the
#    game used, which travels) was built whole before the first frame on an empty Metal cache. An exported app counts both lists and writes pso_prepare_percent= in its config for about 500
#    lines (PlayerPrepare.Percent; the chain's rule 2 honours it). The main app is unchanged.
# 4. The game's language (the owner: the exported South Park started in RUSSIAN although he chose American English in iBuilder). The host's default with no DM_LANG is en-US (hle_oe.c
#    GetDesiredLanguage), i.e. American English: a missing DM_LANG alone does not give Russian, so the Russian text most likely comes from this "(US Uncensored with RUS MOD)" dump itself
#    (its mod replaced texts the American English setting shows; another language row, e.g. British English, would tell) -- NOT VERIFIED. What was wrong and is fixed: the settings sheet only
#    saves values that differ from the row's default, and the row's default is the game's FIRST listed language when American English is not among them (ibuilder-ffi launcher.rs), while the
#    engine then got en-US: the sheet and the game disagreed. Now a game whose language nobody chose (no settings.tsv row, no env.txt line, no harness) starts in the language its sheet
#    SHOWS (settings.rs apply_default_language, after env.txt; logged "game settings: DM_LANG=… (no language chosen: …)"), in iBuilder and in an exported app (settings.tsv and launcher.json
#    travel under ExportedGame/documents/games/<id>/ and are set up in the exported app's Documents at its first launch, never over a choice made there; its settings page edits that copy).
#
# VERIFIED (2026-11-23, M1 Pro): check-patches-apply.sh: every patch 0010-0102 applies in order, no fuzz, no offset; the repository's patches give exactly the compiled tree. Compile
#   (-t:Compile): 0 errors / 40 warnings, the same per file and code as before 0080. Host harness (harness102: … P101;P102): 421 of 421 checks (10 new); 8 of 8 mutations killed. cargo test
#   -p ibuilder-pipeline 270 passed (3 new: tests/default_language.rs), -p ibuilder-ffi 20 passed; clippy -D warnings and fmt clean.
# NOT VERIFIED: nothing ran on a device: an exported app's background preparation and its lock-screen progress, the overlay after a quick boot, the language of this RUS-mod dump.
# NEW UI STRINGS: "Preparing the shaders before the first play: ", " (you can play now; it will stutter until done)", "Shader preparation paused (Resume to go on; you can play now)",
#   "Pause the preparation", "Resume the preparation"; log lines "of another app's shader cache state removed", "this app prepares the game's shaders in the background",
#   "game settings: DM_LANG=" (pipeline).
